sequenceDiagram
  %% The workspace unsaved-work read that Conn's Remove opens (GET /api/v1/conn/instances/{instance}/work, ContainerWorkspaceRead) as a signed executor read (ADR 0267, ADR 0271): the executor action `instance.work_read`, sent as a core NATS request to `orbit.node.<node>.reads` (docs/reference/executor.md#signed-reads). Built; runtime proof pending.
  %% Documented exception: this is a synchronous read and no Operation, so it has no kind of its own. It carries `instance.destroy`, the Operation whose Remove it gates, so instance/destroy.mdx can place it beside instance/container/destroy-engine.mmd.
  %% Answer contract unchanged (docs/reference/development-containers.md#workspace-work-state): state clean, dirty or unknown; unknown carries a reason from stopped, asleep, timeout, not_a_repository, unreachable.
  %% status: built
  %% command: instance:destroy
  %% kind: instance.destroy
  autonumber
  %% lane CLI icon=terminal pill=caller tone=gray
  %% lane GW icon=gateway pill=intent tone=blue
  %% lane EN icon=workflow pill=engine tone=purple
  %% lane N icon=server pill=executor tone=amber
  %% lane C icon=server pill=copy tone=green
  participant CLI as CLI / MCP<br/>orbit · MCP tools
  participant GW as Gateway<br/>Laravel API
  participant EN as Engine<br/>Gateway and NATS
  participant N as app-dev Node<br/>executor
  participant C as Container<br/>via executor
  CLI->>GW: Remove clicked<br/>GET conn/instances/42/work
  %%> Conn reads afresh on every Remove click; no answer is cached or reused
  Note over GW: Resolve the runtime<br/>Node · container · baseline
  %%> The recorded baseline, or the default's container for an Instance without one; the published commits (a task copy's publish)
  alt the Node reports the read action
    %%> The 4 s budget counts from the read's start: the capability lookup (at most 1 s), the content publication and every send end by it, each on a connection of its own, and no reply is taken after it
    %%> No Operation, no lock and no engine decision: the Gateway signs one read order and waits for its reply within the request's 4 s budget
    GW->>EN: Signed read order<br/>machine bus · request
    EN->>N: Read the workspace<br/>read-only · 2 s budget
    %%> Target: Instance 42; the order changes nothing, so the executor writes no journal record, takes no target lock and stores no result; its nonce map still refuses the same order twice
    %%> A recorded baseline and the published commits travel as content the order names by its hash (KV_CONTENT): a baseline may name 2,000 untracked files, beyond the order's 4 KB
    alt Incus reports Running
      N->>C: Git read in /srv/workspace<br/>as agent · no repository code
      %%> The fixed reader of workspace-git-read.py: status, untracked set, stashes, commits beyond the baseline and the published commits; no hooks, no fsmonitor, no write to the index
      %%> Tighter than the SSH reader: every filter driver the configuration names gets empty clean, smudge and process commands, and status does not enter a submodule's work tree (--ignore-submodules=dirty), so no configured program runs; the Node's read also ends by the order's expiry less 0.5 s
      %%> A running copy is always read, also when an asleep marker is present: the marker never hides a dirty workspace
      C-->>N: Status, stashes, commits
      N-->>EN: clean or dirty<br/>counts · names · head
    else not running, asleep marker present
      N-->>EN: unknown · asleep
      %%> As today: the marker only tells asleep from stopped for a copy that is not running; it is not woken to read it
    else not running, no marker
      N-->>EN: unknown · stopped
    end
    EN-->>GW: Reply
    opt the reply is lost
      GW->>EN: Read again<br/>fresh nonce · rest of the budget
      %%> A read has no effect, so a second send is harmless. The first send waits 2.5 s (the Node's 2 s and 0.5 s for the reply); the one re-read gets what is left of the 4 s with a Node budget 0.5 s shorter. A connection that closed after the order went out is a lost reply too. A reply still missing then is `unknown` `timeout`; an order the Node found expired, on arrival or before it ran, is `timeout` too; two sends that both failed to reach the bus are `unreachable`
    end
  else the Node lacks the action
    Note over GW: Read over pinned SSH<br/>ContainerWorkspaceRead
    %%> Today's path, with the same answer shape; nothing else differs
  end
  GW-->>CLI: Work state<br/>clean · dirty · unknown
  %%> `unknown` only for a real read failure (timeout, not_a_repository, unreachable) or the stopped and asleep states above; never for a dirty or clean workspace
  %%> The dialog's answer authorizes nothing: work can change before the user confirms
  CLI->>GW: Remove confirmed<br/>POST conn/instances/42/destroy
  %%> Body `{"acknowledge_unsaved": bool}` (DestroyConnInstanceAction)
  alt acknowledge_unsaved false
    Note over GW: Read the workspace again<br/>the same read, fresh
    %%> ConnInstanceWorkState::assertRemovalSafe: an independent fresh read, by the same executor or SSH path as above, inside this request; still no Operation
    alt the fresh read is clean
      Note over GW: Admit the removal<br/>instance.destroy
      %%> instance/container/destroy-engine.mmd, or instance/destroy.mmd on Swamp
      GW-->>CLI: 202 Accepted<br/>task ID
    else dirty or unknown
      GW--xCLI: 409 instance.unsaved_work<br/>details: the fresh read
      %%> Nothing is recorded; Conn asks again, and only an acknowledged POST removes unsaved work
    end
  else acknowledge_unsaved true
    Note over GW: Admit the removal<br/>no second read
    GW-->>CLI: 202 Accepted<br/>task ID
  end
